[{:db/id 17592186133815 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7ead0ce1-1494-5459-ab15-c85fe87f9dab"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133630 :question/problem "Given the vector ![](images/8f/8f1a6f36da1dacbd3e275372e06e9ff13e7f3600517066116f422d0f8cb00b47.svg), which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $\\mathbf{u}$?\n![](images/c9/c905bc151f6d6df0bfb610152baca3dfe0ff63c4789fa5377de31aa9996da61a.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133770 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a297bc5c-e8a7-5968-a05c-32844e09a57a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133579 :question/problem "If ![](images/55/55d5d5dc4af3eaf8d0bf0474fd77731242346be452c109d6bbc6fdb52033a647.svg) and ![](images/6d/6dc2b50d6bb8a7d2fcc50be918737857d065088320010a356c626e1417efcc82.svg) are orthogonal vectors, find the value of $k.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133771 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c0dbf414-70a0-5f19-8395-cf58e2c89041" "question-4593be43-7c77-5707-9a35-2724546ec310"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133580 :question/problem "Let ![](images/ae/ae5c0c967a0ddd28c163a51aca44edc3340cb76a2f9da28704563b423c591de8.svg) and ![](images/9a/9afd33bf9d62d13ceab462ed9705c007173253b065b347c6475acbff5b8090fe.svg) be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u} \\!\\perp\\! \\mathbf{w}$. Find $(\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v})\\cdot \\mathbf{w} + \\mathbf{u}\\cdot(\\mathbf{v}+ \\mathbf{w}).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133772 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cc095c64-455d-525a-98ca-451d265b041d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133581 :question/problem "Let ![](images/1f/1fb7970633bab3a0518872b1eb14dcfdef5c95f1b6bc01760f4cff1680350413.svg) and ![](images/a1/a1a509e6431cd3b3625d4960bdcd10106da3b60a9d7f7bc9dd11089a6b8960b2.svg) be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=0$. Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -8\\cdot 6+a\\cdot (-15)+b\\cdot 9+(-10)\\cdot (-12) & =0 \\\\ -48-15a+9b+120 & =0 \\\\ -15a+9b & =-72 \\\\ -5a+3b & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{w}=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -8\\cdot 4+a\\cdot 2+b\\cdot (-5)+(-10)\\cdot (-3) & =0 \\\\ -32+2a-5b+30 & =0 \\\\ 2a-5b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-5a+3b=-24 \\\\ 2a-5b=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-10a+6b=-48 \\\\ 10a-25b=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, adding the above equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n-19b = -38 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad b = 2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b = 2$ into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-5(2) & =2 \\\\ 2a-10 & =2 \\\\ 2a & =12 \\\\ a & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b = 6 + 2 = 8.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-7ead0ce1-1494-5459-ab15-c85fe87f9dab" :question/id #uuid "7ead0ce1-1494-5459-ab15-c85fe87f9dab" :question/math-academy-id "q-74086" :question/problem "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3+0-1+2 \\\\  & =-2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =3+0-1-2 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =6+0-2-4 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $w$ and $x$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2093f599-d31a-574d-bf27-4e818cda2660"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2093f599-d31a-574d-bf27-4e818cda2660" :answer-field/id #uuid "2093f599-d31a-574d-bf27-4e818cda2660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-586e0aed-67d2-521e-99a4-464bd6aafb33" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8c854f8c-bc14-576a-8c8c-169fe6f12ace" "answer-1bfdcc5b-d056-5b31-b19a-05f23514f849" "answer-9fd0fd2c-9a26-5e07-8a9b-2801e60a4ff5" "answer-586e0aed-67d2-521e-99a4-464bd6aafb33" "answer-3546e267-373b-5e1e-9457-1de013551d43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c854f8c-bc14-576a-8c8c-169fe6f12ace" :answer/id #uuid "8c854f8c-bc14-576a-8c8c-169fe6f12ace" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ and $w$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bfdcc5b-d056-5b31-b19a-05f23514f849" :answer/id #uuid "1bfdcc5b-d056-5b31-b19a-05f23514f849" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ and $x$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fd0fd2c-9a26-5e07-8a9b-2801e60a4ff5" :answer/id #uuid "9fd0fd2c-9a26-5e07-8a9b-2801e60a4ff5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-586e0aed-67d2-521e-99a4-464bd6aafb33" :answer/id #uuid "586e0aed-67d2-521e-99a4-464bd6aafb33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$w$ and $x$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3546e267-373b-5e1e-9457-1de013551d43" :answer/id #uuid "3546e267-373b-5e1e-9457-1de013551d43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a297bc5c-e8a7-5968-a05c-32844e09a57a" :question/id #uuid "a297bc5c-e8a7-5968-a05c-32844e09a57a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39319" :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ k \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal vectors, then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-3)+k\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-8)+(-6)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-k-16-6 \\\\  & =-k-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-k-7 & =0 \\\\ k & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3e2b0842-7869-5406-b40d-48cd2134b49c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3e2b0842-7869-5406-b40d-48cd2134b49c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e2b0842-7869-5406-b40d-48cd2134b49c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7baae6cc-d820-5841-a12b-4d095c694fc9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f3487e6d-320a-578b-a1e0-1cabee888187" "answer-7baae6cc-d820-5841-a12b-4d095c694fc9" "answer-aa5246e7-ab9c-5a4f-a3c1-b20c8c4b31a2" "answer-b688eeeb-5eaf-5f06-888e-e3443acf2805" "answer-0126d44d-cbd6-5e5d-8f9b-fd5306980a4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3487e6d-320a-578b-a1e0-1cabee888187" :answer/id #uuid "f3487e6d-320a-578b-a1e0-1cabee888187" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7baae6cc-d820-5841-a12b-4d095c694fc9" :answer/id #uuid "7baae6cc-d820-5841-a12b-4d095c694fc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa5246e7-ab9c-5a4f-a3c1-b20c8c4b31a2" :answer/id #uuid "aa5246e7-ab9c-5a4f-a3c1-b20c8c4b31a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b688eeeb-5eaf-5f06-888e-e3443acf2805" :answer/id #uuid "b688eeeb-5eaf-5f06-888e-e3443acf2805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0126d44d-cbd6-5e5d-8f9b-fd5306980a4d" :answer/id #uuid "0126d44d-cbd6-5e5d-8f9b-fd5306980a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c0dbf414-70a0-5f19-8395-cf58e2c89041" :question/id #uuid "c0dbf414-70a0-5f19-8395-cf58e2c89041" :question/math-academy-id "q-74158" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u\\,⊥\\,v.$ Find $(u-2w)\\cdot (w-4v).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot v=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u-2w)\\cdot (w-4v) & =u\\cdot w-2(w\\cdot w)-4(u\\cdot v)+8(w\\cdot v) \\\\  & =u\\cdot w-2(w\\cdot w)+0+8(w\\cdot v) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 3+4\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & -2(3\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & +8(3\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =(3-8-2+6)-2(9+4+1+4)+8(6+2+2+4) \\\\  & =-1-36+112 \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-93222598-353b-55a9-b167-8027058d4fdc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-93222598-353b-55a9-b167-8027058d4fdc" :answer-field/id #uuid "93222598-353b-55a9-b167-8027058d4fdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7a167fdb-738d-5b3d-8284-711c388657bf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c98265c1-02be-53c4-83fe-a4d8b3bf3872" "answer-5ec71bf8-0520-59fa-9854-cb44ec045ef7" "answer-81c9e055-8cf2-5cc9-8653-4e0b2008470e" "answer-7a167fdb-738d-5b3d-8284-711c388657bf" "answer-fc670790-7eab-5b03-aa35-04d8fa5acbac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c98265c1-02be-53c4-83fe-a4d8b3bf3872" :answer/id #uuid "c98265c1-02be-53c4-83fe-a4d8b3bf3872" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ec71bf8-0520-59fa-9854-cb44ec045ef7" :answer/id #uuid "5ec71bf8-0520-59fa-9854-cb44ec045ef7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "112" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81c9e055-8cf2-5cc9-8653-4e0b2008470e" :answer/id #uuid "81c9e055-8cf2-5cc9-8653-4e0b2008470e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a167fdb-738d-5b3d-8284-711c388657bf" :answer/id #uuid "7a167fdb-738d-5b3d-8284-711c388657bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc670790-7eab-5b03-aa35-04d8fa5acbac" :answer/id #uuid "fc670790-7eab-5b03-aa35-04d8fa5acbac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "77" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4593be43-7c77-5707-9a35-2724546ec310" :question/id #uuid "4593be43-7c77-5707-9a35-2724546ec310" :question/math-academy-id "q-74183" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u$ and $w$ are orthogonal. Find $(u+2w)\\cdot (u-4v)-u\\cdot u.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $w$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot w=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u+2w)\\cdot (u-4v)-u\\cdot u & =u\\cdot u+(2w)\\cdot u-u\\cdot (4v)-(2w)\\cdot (4v)-u\\cdot u \\\\  & =2(w\\cdot u)-4(u\\cdot v)-8(w\\cdot v) \\\\  & =0-4(u\\cdot v)-8(w\\cdot v) \\\\  & =-4(u\\cdot v)-8(w\\cdot v) \\\\  & =-4((-5)\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 1) \\\\  & -8(2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3)+8\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-4(-5+9-8+0)-8(2-6-32+3) \\\\  & =16+264 \\\\  & =280.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53026106-93b7-5112-b460-a4866b2a53df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53026106-93b7-5112-b460-a4866b2a53df" :answer-field/id #uuid "53026106-93b7-5112-b460-a4866b2a53df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a0f91a56-bedd-5b8c-8273-1ba24e48d009" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2349f6f7-0b4a-5590-8339-7329d0015da4" "answer-0ab9e3e6-5284-58be-a5fe-0054619d52b2" "answer-a0f91a56-bedd-5b8c-8273-1ba24e48d009" "answer-41f8727d-5688-5fe2-ac9f-115c4c0396ab" "answer-977bcee7-245e-56ff-a839-4b7982e8217d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2349f6f7-0b4a-5590-8339-7329d0015da4" :answer/id #uuid "2349f6f7-0b4a-5590-8339-7329d0015da4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab9e3e6-5284-58be-a5fe-0054619d52b2" :answer/id #uuid "0ab9e3e6-5284-58be-a5fe-0054619d52b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0f91a56-bedd-5b8c-8273-1ba24e48d009" :answer/id #uuid "a0f91a56-bedd-5b8c-8273-1ba24e48d009" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "280" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41f8727d-5688-5fe2-ac9f-115c4c0396ab" :answer/id #uuid "41f8727d-5688-5fe2-ac9f-115c4c0396ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-977bcee7-245e-56ff-a839-4b7982e8217d" :answer/id #uuid "977bcee7-245e-56ff-a839-4b7982e8217d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cc095c64-455d-525a-98ca-451d265b041d" :question/id #uuid "cc095c64-455d-525a-98ca-451d265b041d" :question/math-academy-id "q-39293" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ a \\\\ 7 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u$ is orthogonal to $v$ and $w.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $u$ is orthogonal to $v$ and $w$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1+a\\cdot 4+7\\cdot 0+b\\cdot (-6) & =0 \\\\ 2+4a-6b & =0 \\\\ 4a-6b & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-4)+a\\cdot 3+7\\cdot 5+b\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ -8+3a+35+4b & =0 \\\\ 3a+4b & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4a-6b=-2 \\\\ 3a+4b=-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $-3,$ the second equation by $4,$ and adding the resulting equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n34b=-102\\,⟹\\,b=-3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a-6(-3) & =-2 \\\\ 4a+18 & =-2 \\\\ 4a & =-20 \\\\ a & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b=-5+(-3)=-8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2f630ec-9673-54b1-aa09-9f5f12f9cc84"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2f630ec-9673-54b1-aa09-9f5f12f9cc84" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f630ec-9673-54b1-aa09-9f5f12f9cc84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-314612f9-0892-5598-ae9d-b402b25a618e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1602525e-bf2f-5fd3-827e-a1e276978ea0" "answer-cd646d15-fc68-5176-a821-57dae3be108e" "answer-314612f9-0892-5598-ae9d-b402b25a618e" "answer-2a702037-a4b0-50cc-97fd-b5d6788b58a7" "answer-81fefe85-5730-5d6f-833d-3cdff63a604c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1602525e-bf2f-5fd3-827e-a1e276978ea0" :answer/id #uuid "1602525e-bf2f-5fd3-827e-a1e276978ea0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd646d15-fc68-5176-a821-57dae3be108e" :answer/id #uuid "cd646d15-fc68-5176-a821-57dae3be108e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-314612f9-0892-5598-ae9d-b402b25a618e" :answer/id #uuid "314612f9-0892-5598-ae9d-b402b25a618e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a702037-a4b0-50cc-97fd-b5d6788b58a7" :answer/id #uuid "2a702037-a4b0-50cc-97fd-b5d6788b58a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81fefe85-5730-5d6f-833d-3cdff63a604c" :answer/id #uuid "81fefe85-5730-5d6f-833d-3cdff63a604c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134252 :question/worked-solution "Given that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 3+a\\cdot 4+b\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ -9+4a+b-4 & =0 \\\\ 4a+b & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 1+a\\cdot 1+b\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ -3+a-3b+16 & =0 \\\\ a-3b & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4a+b=13 \\\\ a-3b=-13\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13a=26\\,⟹\\,a=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)+b & =13 \\\\ 8+b & =13 \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b=2+5=7.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135037 :tutorial/content "Let $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ be vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^n$. What do we mean when we say that the vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ are orthogonal?\n\nTwo vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ are **orthogonal** if their dot product equals zero: \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=0\n$$\n\nIf two vectors are orthogonal, then we denote this by $\\mathbf{u} \\!\\perp\\! \\mathbf{v}$. For instance, the vectors \n\n![](images/29/29a81db4068e5bcc97fd38729ca19f11988a08e905bfc189e69c88357185ea31.svg)\n\nin $\\mathbb{R^2}$ are orthogonal, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{1}\\cdot {e}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0+0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** The zero vector $\\mathbf{0}$ is orthogonal to any vector $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$ since $\\mathbf{0}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}=0$." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133986 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
